**Structural answer and validation.** Psi<=0 does **not** hold identically. The engine is not additively separable across users. Occupancy changes target modes and TDM airtime; RF power is solved with cross-beam coupling; payload energy includes nonlinear PA supply power and shared activation costs. Even independent beam resolution would not imply zero Psi when two users affect the same beam. Additivity would require each user's contribution to depend only on that user's own action, which these executed examples directly disprove.

